{number: 102}
{title: In the Garden}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
I [C] come to the garden alone,
While the dew is still on the [F] roses,
And the [G7] voice I hear falling [C] on my ear,
The [D7] Son of God dis-[G7] closes.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
And He [C] walks with me, and He [G7] talks with me,
And He tells me I am His [C] own;
And the [E7] joy we [Am] share as we [C] tarry there,
None [G7] other has ever [C] known.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
He [C] speaks, and the sound of His voice,
Is so sweet the birds hush their [F] singing,
And the [G7] melody that He [C] gave to me
With-[D7] in my heart is [G7] ringing.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
I’d [C] stay in the garden with Him
Though the night around me be [F] falling,
But He [G7] bids me go; thru the [C] voice of woe
His [D7] voice to me is [G7] calling.
{end_of_verse}
